    body: "Vamanan is the dwarf incarnation of Lord Vishnu, the fifth of the ten Dashavatara avatars. He appeared during the reign of the benevolent asura king Mahabali to restore the cosmic balance that the king's growing pride had disturbed. Vamanan appears small, almost overlooked — a short brahmachari (celibate student) carrying a wooden umbrella and a kamandalu (water pot). Yet within that humble form burns the full power of Vishnu, the preserver of the universe. The story of Vamanan is the story of how the smallest gesture can hold the largest meaning: how a dwarf's request for three paces of land became the moment the infinite revealed itself through the finite.",
