    body: "King Mahabali ruled the three worlds with such generosity and justice that even the gods grew uneasy. His subjects adored him; there was no lie, no poverty, no fear under his reign. But his fame and power had grown so vast that Indra, king of the gods, felt his own throne tremble. The gods appealed to Lord Vishnu for help.\n\nVishnu was born as Vamanan — a dwarf brahmachari, no taller than a young boy. He arrived at the great yajna (sacrifice) where Bali was granting boons to all who came. The small sage asked for just three paces of land, measured by his own tiny feet. Bali's guru, Shukracharya, recognized the dwarf as Vishnu himself and warned the king not to grant the request. But Bali had given his word — and a king who breaks his promise is no king at all.\n\nThe moment Bali poured the ceremonial water granting the boon, Vamanan began to grow. He expanded into Trivikrama, the cosmic giant. With his first stride he covered the entire earth. With his second, he reached the heavens and the space beyond. For the third stride, there was nowhere left to step. Bali, understanding at last, knelt and offered his own head. Vamanan placed his foot upon it and sent the king to Sutala, the netherworld — not as punishment, but as honor. Bali was beloved forever, and granted the boon of returning to his people once a year: that return is Onam.",
