    body: "Vamanan is the fifth avatar of the Dashavatara — the ten incarnations of Lord Vishnu, each appearing at a moment of cosmic crisis to restore dharma. The ten avatars are: Matsya (fish), Kurma (turtle), Varaha (boar), Narasimha (man-lion), Vamana (dwarf), Parashurama, Rama, Krishna, Buddha (or Balarama, depending on tradition), and Kalki.\n\nVamanan is unique among them because he conquers without a weapon, without an army, without anger. His only instrument is a request, and his only force is truth. Where other avatars wield swords, bows, or chakras, Vamanan wields a request for three paces of land. In his dwarf form he is Vamanan; in his cosmic, all-spanning form he is Trivikrama, 'the one who took three steps.'\n\nThe avatar teaches that divine power does not always arrive with thunder — sometimes it comes as a small figure at the door, asking for almost nothing. The power is not in the size of the form but in the truth of the purpose.",
