    body: "Onappattu (Onam songs) are an essential part of Onam celebrations, sung during pookkalam arrangements, kaikottikali dances, and family gatherings. Here is a traditional Onam song in Malayalam:\n\nഓണം വന്നു ഓണായിട്ട്\nഓണം കിളിക്കാവിൽ പൂത്ത്\nമാവേലി നാട് വാണീടും കാലം\nമനുഷ്യർ സുഖമുള്ള കാലം\n\n(Onam vannu onnaayittu\nOnam kilikkaavil poothu\nMaaveli naadu vaaneedum kaalam\nManushyar sukhamulla kaalam)\n\nTranslation: 'Onam has come, Onam has bloomed in the kilikkaavu tree. The time when Maveli ruled the land — the time when all people were happy.'\n\nThe most famous Onam song is 'Maveli Naadu Vaneedum Kalam,' which describes Mahabali's golden reign:\n\nമാവേലി നാട് വാണീടും കാലം\nമനുഷ്യർ സുഖമുള്ള കാലം\nആടും കലകളും ആടിയാടി\nപാടും പാട്ടുകൾ പാടിപ്പാടി\n\nTranslation: 'When Maveli ruled the land, the people were happy. Dances and arts performed freely, songs were sung endlessly.'\n\nThese songs are not just music — they are oral history, keeping the memory of a beloved king alive across generations.",
