    body: "The Dashavatara are the ten primary incarnations of Lord Vishnu, each appearing to restore cosmic order (dharma) when it is threatened. They are, in order:\n\n1. Matsya (Fish) — Saved the first man, Manu, from a great deluge.\n\n2. Kurma (Turtle) — Supported Mount Mandara during the churning of the ocean of milk.\n\n3. Varaha (Boar) — Lifted the earth from the cosmic waters when the demon Hiranyaksha hid it.\n\n4. Narasimha (Man-Lion) — Destroyed the demon Hiranyakashipu to protect his devotee Prahlada.\n\n5. Vamana (Dwarf) — The avatar this GPT is about! Restored cosmic balance by humbling Mahabali's pride.\n\n6. Parashurama (Rama with an axe) — A warrior sage who cleared the earth of corrupt kings 21 times.\n\n7. Rama — The prince of Ayodhya, hero of the Ramayana.\n\n8. Krishna — The divine cowherd, charioteer of the Bhagavad Gita, and one of the most beloved deities.\n\n9. Buddha (or Balarama, depending on tradition) — The enlightened one.\n\n10. Kalki — The future avatar, who will appear at the end of the current age (Kali Yuga) to restore dharma.\n\nVamanan sits in the middle of this sequence — the pivot point — and is the only avatar who conquers through a request rather than force.",
