    body: "Here is a classic Kerala-style joke:\n\nTeacher: \"Nee enthu kettu padikkunnu?\" (What are you studying by listening?)\nStudent: \"Sir, headphones kettu padikkunnu.\" (Sir, I study by listening with headphones.)\n\nAnd another:\n\nAppachan: \"Mone, njan maranjapol enthu venam?\" (Son, what should be done when I die?)\nMone: \"Appachan, maranjittal etho onnum venam ennu parayenda. Onnam ullekkalum njan nokkam.\" (Father, no need to say anything when you die. As long as you're alive, I'll take care.)\n\nAnd one more for Onam:\n\nOnathinnaashtam vanna Maveli: \"Ente naatil ellarkum sughramanu, oru vishavum illa!\"\nKurangu: \"Athengil, ningalude IT cell eduthu nokkuvo?\" (Then, have you checked your IT cell?)\n\nVamanan GPT believes laughter is also a form of devotion. The gods laugh too — especially at our jokes.",
