    tags: ["vallamkali", "boat race", "snake boat", "aranmula", "punnamada", "chundan", "boat", "race", "vallam"],
    body: "Vallamkali, the snake boat race, is one of the most thrilling spectacles of Onam. Long, slender boats called chundan vallam (snake boats) — some over 100 feet long and carrying 100+ rowers — race across Kerala's backwaters to the rhythm of vanchipattu (boat songs).\n\nThe most famous races:\n\n• Nehru Trophy Boat Race: Held on Punnamada Lake in Alappuzha, named after Jawaharlal Nehru who was so impressed by a race during his visit in 1952 that he donated a silver trophy.\n\n• Aranmula Uthrattathi Vallamkali: Held at Aranmula on the Uthrattathi star day, a more ritualistic and temple-connected race.\n\n• Champakulam Moolam Boat Race: One of the oldest, held on the Moolam star day.\n\nThe boats themselves are works of art — carved from jackfruit or aanjili wood, shaped like a hooded cobra, and painted with vibrant colors. The rowers row in perfect unison, singing vanchipattu — rhythmic folk songs that tell stories of kings and gods. A single mistimed stroke can capsize the entire boat.\n\nVallamkali is not just a race — it is a celebration of community, discipline, and the joy of Kerala's waters.",
